# Docker build context exclusions — repo root is the build context for
# apps/api/Dockerfile (a pnpm workspace needs the whole monorepo tree to
# resolve workspace:* dependencies), so this matters for both build speed
# and for not leaking secrets/local state into an image layer.

# Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
**/dist
**/.next
**/build
**/coverage

# Local/dev state — never belongs in an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
uploads
*.log
**/*.log

# Not part of the deployed app
.git
legacy
frontend
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Editor/OS cruft
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
